---
kind: scene
id: road.crossing
title: The far bank
on: chapterEnd
after: 'visited("bridge.arrival")'
---

## The Far Bank

::bg{location="far_bank" time="dawn"}
::music{action="change" mood="peaceful" volume="normal"}
/* chapterEnd is `judge: before`: the quests are settled when this plays, so the
   epilogue reads how they ended instead of re-deriving it from state. */
<match on="quest.emberRoad.failedBy">
  <when is="by">
    @narrator: The fourth night came and the chain did not. Brannoc turns the wagons for Ostwick. The Company does not pay for maybes.
  </when>
  <when is="fail">
    @narrator: What is left of the caravan limps back toward Harrow's Ford. The far bank stays far.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    <match on="run.bridge">
      <when is="parleyed">
        @narrator: The chain came down at dawn without a shot fired. Maelis stood aside on the near arch with the proof inside her coat, and counted the wagons as they passed. {{run.wagons:plural(One|#Word)}}.
        @maelis: Tell Ostwick the Duskbound can read, Warden.
      </when>
      <when is="paid">
        @narrator: The Duskbound let you through with the Company's strongbox on their shoulders. Brannoc rode the whole crossing without a word, which from Brannoc is a speech.
        @brannoc: The Company will hear what you did with its money. From me.
      </when>
      <when is="sold">
        @narrator: The Duskbound waved you across. They were in a hurry. They had somewhere to be, back at the ford.
      </when>
      <when is="stormed">
        @narrator: The wagons crossed over the cut chain and the crossbows no one would pick up again. Eleven wagons. Fewer drivers.
      </when>
      <when is="held">
        @narrator: The chain is still up. Nobody on the far bank is expecting you.
      </when>
    </match>
  </otherwise>
</match>
@narrator{when="quest.parley.failedBy == 'superseded'"}: Maelis never got her proof. Coldwater stays off the map.
@corvin{when="quest.toll.failedBy == 'superseded' && holds(inParty(corvin))"}: Three deserters and a sack of silver, and we walked past them. I'll be bringing that up.
@isolde{when="quest.isoldeOath.state == 'complete' && holds(inParty(isolde))"}: I swore at Coldwater I'd never again stand by and call it orders. Thank you for not making me a liar.

@narrator{when="run.hostagesFreed"}: Behind you at the ford, a miller is teaching two children to curse the Company properly.
@narrator{when="!run.hostagesFreed && quest.hostages.state == 'failed'"}: Nobody at the ford will say where Pell and Hanne were taken. Nobody asks you.
@narrator{when="holds(hostile(marrow))"}: The Marrow folk will not forget whose wagons came through their ford, or what was sold to pay for the crossing.
@narrator{when="holds(sidedWith(dusk))"}: On the parapet a Duskbound crossbowman lifts his bow as the last wagon passes. A salute, of a kind.
@narrator{when="holds(hostile(company))"}: The Ashen Company will want its strongbox back, and it knows your name.
@narrator{when="holds(departed(wren))"}: Wren's pack is not on the last wagon. You keep looking for it anyway.
@wren{when="@wrenWithUs && holds(knows(token))"}: Hold the wagon a moment. There. Tam's token, on the far side. He always wanted to see it.
@narrator{when="count(loyal(_)) >= 2"}: Whatever the Company says about this crossing, the people around your fire will say something else.
@narrator{when="quest.emberRoad.state == 'complete'"}: {{run.wagons:plural(One wagon|#Word wagons)}} on the far bank. Brannoc counts them twice, and does not count the people.
::set{user.chaptersCleared += 1}
